exports[`B1 main inventories (a4be19d5b) > preserves socket verbs, public verbs, and all public help > help 1`] = `
{
  "app": "Usage: dohc app <verb> [arguments] [options]

Approve, open, and share apps.

Verbs:
  listLocal            List an app's publications on this computer.
  prepareLocal         Prepare an app to open on this computer.
  launchLocal          Get a local URL for an approved app.
  list                 List an app's shared publications.
  prepare              Prepare an app for a share link.
  approve              Publish a prepared app.
  cancel               Discard a prepared app before approval.
  withdraw             Stop a shared publication.
  revokeCollection     Remove a shared publication's Collection access.
  reviewReactivation   Prepare a stopped publication to publish again.
  responses            List responses link holders sent through a share link.
  undo-responses       Remove responses link holders sent through a share link.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.

Run dohc app <verb> --help to see its arguments and options.
",
  "app approve": "Usage: dohc app approve '<JSON>' [options]

Publish a prepared app.

Fields: workspaceId, approvalId, candidateDigest
Optional fields: linkReads
Take approvalId and candidateDigest from prepare, prepareLocal, or
reviewReactivation.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app cancel": "Usage: dohc app cancel '<JSON>' [options]

Discard a prepared app before approval.

Fields: workspaceId, approvalId

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app launchLocal": "Usage: dohc app launchLocal '<JSON>' [options]

Get a local URL for an approved app.

Fields: workspaceId, publicationId
The URL works on this computer while dohc is open. It is not a share link.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app list": "Usage: dohc app list '<JSON>' [options]

List an app's shared publications.

Fields: workspaceId, appRoot
Optional fields: cursor

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app listLocal": "Usage: dohc app listLocal '<JSON>' [options]

List an app's publications on this computer.

Fields: workspaceId, appRoot

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app prepare": "Usage: dohc app prepare '<JSON>' [options]

Prepare an app for a share link.

Fields: workspaceId, appRoot, shareId, grantId
shareId and grantId name the share and its link grant. Review the result, then
approve.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app prepareLocal": "Usage: dohc app prepareLocal '<JSON>' [options]

Prepare an app to open on this computer.

Fields: workspaceId, appRoot
Review the source and the dataset operations it asks for, then approve.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app responses": "Usage: dohc app responses '<JSON>' [options]

List responses link holders sent through a share link.

Fields: workspaceId, grantId
Optional fields: publicPrincipalId, afterAcceptanceId, limit

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app reviewReactivation": "Usage: dohc app reviewReactivation '<JSON>' [options]

Prepare a stopped publication to publish again.

Fields: workspaceId, publicationId
Review the result, then approve.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app revokeCollection": "Usage: dohc app revokeCollection '<JSON>' [options]

Remove a shared publication's Collection access.

Fields: workspaceId, publicationId, expectedAuthorityRevision
Set publicationId to publications[].publicationId from list.
Set expectedAuthorityRevision to publications[].authorityRevision from list.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app undo-responses": "Usage: dohc app undo-responses '<JSON>' [options]

Remove responses link holders sent through a share link.

Fields: workspaceId, grantId, operationId
Optional fields: publicPrincipalId, afterAcceptanceId, limit
operationId names this removal. Retry failed items with the same operationId.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "app withdraw": "Usage: dohc app withdraw '<JSON>' [options]

Stop a shared publication.

Fields: workspaceId, publicationId, expectedAuthorityRevision
Set publicationId to publications[].publicationId from list.
Set expectedAuthorityRevision to publications[].authorityRevision from list.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Each verb takes one JSON object that names workspaceId. Find workspaceId in
.dohc/manifest.json at the workspace root.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "automation": "Usage: dohc automation <verb> [arguments] [options]

Press Button fields, read an automation's runs, and try a failed run again.

Verbs:
  list      Read a Collection's automation definitions and on/off file state.
  switch    Switch one automation on or off in its file.
  buttons   Inspect Button fields and the actions they require you to confirm.
  runs      List an automation's runs on this computer, newest first.
  run       Show one run: what started it, what each step changed, and why it
            failed.
  retry     Try a failed run again. It resumes after the last step that
            finished.
  press     Press a Button field on one record, as a person clicks it in dohc.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.

Run dohc automation <verb> --help to see its arguments and options.
",
  "automation buttons": "Usage: dohc automation buttons <collection> [options]

Inspect Button fields and the actions they require you to confirm.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --table <table>   Inspect the buttons in this dataset table.
  --as-agent        Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json            Print the result as JSON.
  --help            Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "automation list": "Usage: dohc automation list <collection> [options]

Read a Collection's automation definitions and on/off file state.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "automation press": "Usage: dohc automation press <collection> <button> <record> [options]

Press a Button field on one record, as a person clicks it in dohc.

Name the record by its id, or a dataset record by its primary key as JSON.
The press prints the id of the run it started. Follow it with automation run.
With --as-agent, the press is recorded as the agent's, for you. A press from an
agent run that an automation started is the agent's too, and counts in that
chain of automations, which stops after 4 steps.
In a shared view, a press goes to the owner's computer, which runs it, as in
dohc.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --table <table>      Name the table when the button is in more than one table
                       of a dataset Collection.
  --confirm <action>   Run this action, which dohc cannot undo. The press names
                       each action it would run. Repeat for more actions.
  --request-id <id>    Send the same id again, after a timeout for example, to
                       get the same press instead of a second one.
  --as-agent           Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json               Print the result as JSON.
  --help               Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "automation retry": "Usage: dohc automation retry <collection> <automation> <run> [options]

Try a failed run again. It resumes after the last step that finished.

Only the computer that ran it can try a run again. Anywhere else, the command
names that computer.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --start-over   Run it from the first step when the automation changed since
                 the run failed. This can repeat changes the run already made.
  --as-agent     Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json         Print the result as JSON.
  --help         Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "automation run": "Usage: dohc automation run <collection> <automation> <run> [options]

Show one run: what started it, what each step changed, and why it failed.

Steps count from 1 in the order automations.yaml lists them, including the steps
inside if and otherwise. A step that changed nothing is not listed.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "automation runs": "Usage: dohc automation runs <collection> <automation> [options]

List an automation's runs on this computer, newest first.

Lists 20 runs at a time, newest first, as the Automations panel does. Each line
starts with the run's ID.
When older runs remain, the last line gives the --page value that lists them.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --page <page>   List the older runs the last line of an earlier listing names.
  --as-agent      Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json          Print the result as JSON.
  --help          Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "automation switch": "Usage: dohc automation switch <collection> <automation> <on|off> [options]

Switch one automation on or off in its file.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Collection by its folder in the workspace, and an automation by its id in
the Collection's automations.yaml.
Each computer keeps the runs of the automations it ran. Try again follows the
same rules as in dohc.

Options:
  --base <hash>      Use the contentHash returned by automation list.
  --submit-id <id>   Identify this switch. After an unknown save, read
                     definitions and sync state before retrying.
  --reformat         Confirm losing comments and hand formatting in
                     automations.yaml.
  --as-agent         Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json             Print the result as JSON.
  --help             Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "chat": "Usage: dohc chat <verb> [arguments] [options]

Read and post in Groups and threads.

Verbs:
  groups    List the Groups in this workspace.
  threads   List the threads in a Group.
  inbox     List unread threads. For an agent, also list its unread mentions.
  show      Show a thread or message and mark the thread read.
  post      Start a thread in a Group.
  reply     Reply in a thread.
  react     Add your reaction to a message, or remove it if it is already there.
  grep      Search message text and thread titles.
  export    Save threads as Markdown files, one file per thread.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Group by its name or ID, and a thread or message by its ID. A unique ID
prefix also works.
DOHC_CHAT_ACTOR=agent in the environment does the same as --as-agent.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.

Run dohc chat <verb> --help to see its arguments and options.
",
  "chat export": "Usage: dohc chat export [options]

Save threads as Markdown files, one file per thread.

Use at most one of --all, --group, or --thread.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Group by its name or ID, and a thread or message by its ID. A unique ID
prefix also works.
DOHC_CHAT_ACTOR=agent in the environment does the same as --as-agent.

Options:
  --out <folder>      Write the files to this folder. Required.
  --all               Export every thread. This is the default.
  --group <group>     Export the threads in one Group.
  --thread <thread>   Export one thread.
  --as-agent          Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json              Print the result as JSON.
  --help              Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "chat grep": "Usage: dohc chat grep <pattern> [options]

Search message text and thread titles.

Put options first, then --, then text that starts with a dash.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Name a Group by its name or ID, and a thread or message by its ID. A unique ID
prefix also works.
DOHC_CHAT_ACTOR=agent in the environment does the same as --as-agent.

Options:
  --group <group>     Search only this Group.
  --thread <thread>   Search only this thread.
  --from <author>     Match authors: human, agent, or part of a name.
  --since <when>      Match messages newer than a date or an age such as 7d.
  -i                  Ignore case. Without it, a regex or a pattern with
                      capitals matches case.
  -l                  Print only the IDs of threads that match.
  -C <count>          Show this many messages before and after each match.
  --limit <count>     Print at most this many results. The default is 100.
  --regex             Read the pattern as a regular expression.
  --as-agent          Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json              Print the result as JSON.
  --help              Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "chat groups": "Usage: dohc chat groups [options]

