  "document": "Usage: dohc document <verb> [arguments] [options]

Read, edit, and create live Markdown documents.

Verbs:
  read     Read the current Markdown, including edits in an open editor.
  edit     Replace matching text or append Markdown through the live document.
  create   Create a Markdown document without overwriting an existing file.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Paths resolve from your current folder. Changes are recorded as an agent's, as
with MCP.
A refusal exits with status 1 and prints its reason to stderr, including with
--json.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.

Run dohc document <verb> --help to see its arguments and options.
",
  "document create": "Usage: dohc document create <path> [-] [options]

Create a Markdown document without overwriting an existing file.

Use - as the body to read it from stdin.
Use --text instead to supply Markdown. With neither, create an empty document.
The path must end in .md or .markdown. Frontmatter is refused.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Paths resolve from your current folder. Changes are recorded as an agent's, as
with MCP.
A refusal exits with status 1 and prints its reason to stderr, including with
--json.

Options:
  --text <markdown>   Use this Markdown as the body. An empty string is allowed.
  --agent <name>      Record this agent name with the change.
  --as-agent          Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json              Print the result as JSON.
  --help              Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "document edit": "Usage: dohc document edit <path> [-] [options]

Replace matching text or append Markdown through the live document.

Use - as the body to read it from stdin.
Use --text instead to supply the body as an argument. Each side allows at most
256 KiB of UTF-8.
Edits change the body, not frontmatter. Concurrent editing can prevent removing
blocks or changing their kind.
Read again after a warning or an unexplained failure. Retry keys have the same
limits as dohc_edit_document.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Paths resolve from your current folder. Changes are recorded as an agent's, as
with MCP.
A refusal exits with status 1 and prints its reason to stderr, including with
--json.

Options:
  --text <markdown>    Use this Markdown as the body. An empty string is
                       allowed.
  --agent <name>       Record this agent name with the change.
  --find <markdown>    Replace this exact, unique match. Omit to append.
  --request-id <key>   Reuse this key when retrying the same edit, as with
                       dohc_edit_document.
  --as-agent           Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json               Print the result as JSON.
  --help               Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "document read": "Usage: dohc document read <path> [options]

Read the current Markdown, including edits in an open editor.

Read before editing. Without --json, prints the Markdown byte for byte.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Paths resolve from your current folder. Changes are recorded as an agent's, as
with MCP.
A refusal exits with status 1 and prints its reason to stderr, including with
--json.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "history": "Usage: dohc history <verb> [arguments] [options]

Read the changes History records for files.

Verbs:
  list   List changes to files, newest first.
  show   Print a file's text as one change left it.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Changes come from the active version of the workspace.

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.

Run dohc history <verb> --help to see its arguments and options.
",
  "history list": "Usage: dohc history list [<path>] [options]

List changes to files, newest first.

With a path, list that file's own changes, across its renames. Each line starts
with the change's ID.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Changes come from the active version of the workspace.

Options:
  --limit <count>   List at most this many changes. The default is 50, the most
                    500.
  --as-agent        Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json            Print the result as JSON.
  --help            Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "history show": "Usage: dohc history show <change> [options]

Print a file's text as one change left it.

Find the change's ID with history list. With --json, print both sides and the
change's details.

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.
Changes come from the active version of the workspace.

Options:
  --before     Print the text from before the change instead.
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.
",
  "top": "Usage: dohc <command> <verb> [arguments] [options]

Run dohc inside a workspace folder while the dohc app is open.

Commands:
  document     Read, edit, and create live Markdown documents.
               read, edit, create
  chat         Read and post in Groups and threads.
               groups, threads, inbox, show, post, reply, react, grep, export
  dataset      Create, change, and use transactional Collections.
               list, describe, history, historyRevision, prepareHistoryRestore,
               permissions, setGrant, removeGrant, lifecycle, archive, restore,
               deletePreview, delete, pendingAttempts, reconcileAttempt,
               cancelAttempt, export, prepareRecovery, claimRecovery,
               discardRecovery, upload, file, createForm,
               prepareRelationChoices, create, prepare, approve, discard,
               prepareMigration, migrationPreviewPage, prepareSchemaChange,
               approveMigration, discardMigration, invoke
  app          Approve, open, and share apps.
               listLocal, prepareLocal, launchLocal, list, prepare, approve,
               cancel, withdraw, revokeCollection, reviewReactivation,
               responses, undo-responses
  history      Read the changes History records for files.
               list, show
  automation   Press Button fields, read an automation's runs, and try a failed
               run again.
               list, switch, buttons, runs, run, retry, press

Options:
  --as-agent   Post and read chat as an agent.
  --json       Print the result as JSON.
  --help       Show help. -h does the same.

Run dohc <command> --help to see what each verb does.
",
}
`;

